      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "The formula $V(t)=100\\cdot {4}^{t}$ gives the number of times a video has been reproduced $t$ hours after it was published. How many reproductions will the video have after $6$ hours?",
      "worked_solution": "To get the number of reproductions after $6$ hours, we evaluate the function at $t=6.$ Substituting $t=6$ into the function $V(t)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V(6) & =100\\cdot {4}^{6} \\\\  & =100\\cdot 4\\,096 \\\\  & =409\\,600.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, after $6$ hours, the video will have $409\\,600$ reproductions.",
